The problem is, of course, the uncertainty about the semantics of mass noun=
s.  I think that Lojban can find expressions that work more or less like ma=
ss nouns, while remaining count at their heart.  The other approach, which =
does turn up in Lojban already is to take mass "nouns" as "adjectives": the=
 first definition of {djacu} is "made of water", the last is "aqueous".  We=
 rarely
worry about what {lo redro} might mean with quantifiers attached, though it=
 raises similar problems to {lo djacu}.=20

